    "body": "Wait... Why there is `padding`? It seems to me this doesn't match impl of Blink and WebKit. Or is that added later than their implementations? Would adding that causes compat issues?\n\nAlso what exactly is the default rendering in your mind about `<details>` / `<summary>`? Is it\n\n```\nv summary\n  some more details\n```\n\nor\n\n```\nv summary\nsome more details\n```\n\nFor the second one (which is what Chrome and Safari show to me), we would need `list-style: disclosure-* inside` as mentioned by @takenspc in #722, and the padding doesn't seem to be something sensible. If you actually want the first one, then we do not need the `inside` keyword, and yes we should move the padding into the style. It should be `padding-inline-start: 40px` in that case.\n",
